<h5 class="activityhead">Vacation Class 2017</h5>
<p style="text-align: justify;padding-left:200px;padding-right: 200px;">A series of workshop was conducted during vacation of S4 and s2 Students 
    <br>In AutoCAD workshop various tools and models were taught and practice on various models were done. The resource persons were Ragesh R, Mohammed Shebin, Mohammed & Aneez A and was conducted on 19th and 20th june 2017
    <br>In Solidworks workshop various tools for modeling, assembly and animation were taught and practiced. The resource persons were Ragesh R, Mohammed Shebin , Mohammed & Aneez A and  was conducted on 21st and 22nd june 2017
    <br>The workshop on C programming covered the basics and the students were made to program by themselves after making them aware ofthe basic programming thoroughly. The resource persons were Johnny & Ajai. The workshop was conducted on 28th& 29th June 2017.
    <br>In Basics ofArduino,programming basics were taught along with different sensors. The resource person was Archa Mohan. The workshops were on 5th July to 6th July 2017.
    <br>Proteus workshop was conductedon 7 July 2017. The basics of drawing and simulating circuits in the software were taught. Also, basics of digital electronics and how to add Arduino library in Proteus were taught. The resource persons were Archa Mohan.
    <br>Basics of Matlab were conducted on  13th  to 14thJuly 2017.The resource persons were Archa Mohan and Priya Jose. The workshops covered thebasics and enabled the students with the different applications of both software for mathematical and different applications.
    <br>Basics of Scilab were conducted on  27thJuly 2017 respectively. The resource persons were Archa Mohan. The workshop covered thebasics and enabled the students with the different applications of the software for mathematical and different applications.
    <br>Java workshop was intended to enable the students to strengthen their basics on Java programming. The class was conducted by Ms.Merlin on 10th to 11th July 2017.
    </p>
